 "plan_effect_reason_en": "Keep this line: HUS's pages say fitness can rule out lung cancer surgery and that doctors refer cancer patients to physiotherapy when needed, but none describes an exercise test, a geriatric assessment or a four-week prehabilitation programme followed by a second decision.",
 "verdict_en": "No public sign that it is running in East Uusimaa. Evidence supports that it works, but not the size of effect we assume. Supported: A 2022 Cochrane review (10 randomised trials, 636 patients) found that exercise before surgery cut lung complications after surgery (risk ratio 0.45) and shortened the hospital stay by about 2.2 days. Not supported: No page I read measures how many more patients receive curative-intent treatment after prehabilitation, so the assumed 0.5-point gain is not shown.",
